/*
 * sprites.js - every frame of Pip, as plain readable data.
 *
 * Each frame is 64 strings of 64 characters. Every character is a
 * palette key from palettes.js and "." means transparent. Frames are drawn
 * facing right; the renderer flips them horizontally to face left.
 *
 * DETAIL is how many sprite pixels make up one of Pip's original 32-grid
 * units. The renderer sizes Pip in those units, so a finer grid adds detail
 * without making him any bigger on screen.
 *
 * Generated by tools/gen-sprites.js from tools/frame-specs.js.
 * You can edit any frame here by hand - this file is the source of truth
 * at runtime. Re-running "npm run sprites" regenerates the whole file, so
 * fold hand edits back into frame-specs.js if you want to keep using it.
 */

